.TH INIT 8 "August 4, 2026" "ReBSD" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
init, telinit \- System V process initialization and runlevel control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /sbin/init
[
.B \-s
]
.br
.B /etc/init
.I runlevel
.br
.B /etc/telinit
.I runlevel
.SH DESCRIPTION
When invoked as process 1,
.B init
reads
.IR /etc/inittab ,
runs every
.B sysinit
entry in file order before opening the console, selects the configured
default runlevel, and supervises the processes selected for that level.
The first transition from single-user state to a multi-user runlevel runs
the matching
.B boot
and
.B bootwait
entries before the ordinary entries for that level.
.PP
Runlevels
.B 0
through
.B 6
and
.B S
are real operating states.  The
.BR a ,
.BR b ,
and
.B c
levels are on-demand states and do not replace the current runlevel.
The
.B \-s
option overrides the configured default and enters single-user mode.
.PP
When invoked by the super-user with a process ID other than 1,
.B init
and
.B telinit
send the requested state to process 1 using the traditional System V
signal interface.  The following requests are accepted:
.TP
.B 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 S s
Enter the selected runlevel.
.TP
.B a b c
Start matching on-demand entries without changing the current runlevel.
.TP
.B Q q
Re-read
.IR /etc/inittab .
Running entries with the same identifier continue until they exit, so a
changed command is used on its next spawn.  Removed and
.B off
entries are stopped, and newly enabled entries are started.
.PP
Before stopping a supervised process,
.B init
sends
.B SIGTERM
to its process group, waits five seconds, and then sends
.B SIGKILL
if necessary.  A respawn entry that starts ten times within two minutes is
disabled for five minutes.  A runlevel request or
.B Q
request clears this throttle.
.PP
On
.BR SIGPWR ,
.B init
runs the configured entries whose runlevels include the current state:
.B powerfail
and
.B powerwait
actions.
.PP
There is deliberately no Linux
.I initctl
FIFO or Linux init control ABI.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/inittab
Process and runlevel configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/rc.sysinit
Machine initialization selected by the default ReBSD inittab.
.TP
.I /etc/rc
Runlevel dispatcher.
.TP
.I /etc/rcN.d
Runlevel scripts.
.TP
.I /dev/console
Initialization diagnostics and single-user console.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kill (1),
.BR sh (1),
.BR inittab (5),
.BR getty (8),
.BR halt (8),
.BR reboot (8),
.BR shutdown (8)
